PODFoam_Debug, APMOSFoam, AEFoam: NumPy owns each snapshot too

The three solvers passed PyArray_SimpleNewFromData over the reused C++
buffer input_vals, so a view the module kept read the next step's
values. Their shipped modules kept the first snapshot of each window
that way, and the first two snapshot columns came out equal; in AEFoam
they were rows. PyArray_SimpleNew plus a copy of the buffer gives Python
an owning array. A failed allocation stops the run with a message.
Nothing else in the three solvers changes.

